<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the box office over the Friday-to-Sunday weekend, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc.</p>
<p>Final data are due Monday. (Rank last week in parentheses).</p>
<p>    1=(1) Beverly Hills Ninja .............. $5.9 million</p>
<p>    1=(5) Jerry Maguire .................... $5.9 million</p>
<p>    1=(*) In Love And War .................. $5.9 million</p>
<p>    4 (2) Metro ............................ $5.6 million</p>
<p>    5 (3) Evita ............................ $5.5 million</p>
<p>    6 (6) Scream ........................... $4.4 million</p>
<p>    7 (4) The Relic ........................ $4.2 million</p>
<p>    8 (*) Fierce Creatures ................. $4.0 million</p>
<p>    9 (7) Michael .......................... $3.7 million</p>
<p>    10(*) Zeus and Roxanne ................. $2.9 million</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Beverly Hills Ninja&quot; and &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; are released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;In Love and War&quot; and &quot;Michael&quot; are released by New Line Cinema, both units of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Metro&quot; and &quot;Evita&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co. .</p>
<p>&quot;Scream&quot; is released by Disney-owned Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;The Relic&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Fierce Creatures&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Zeus and Roxanne&quot; is released by MGM, which is owned by financier Kirk Kerkorian and Australia's Seven Network Ltd..</p>
